+## 2026-10-04 repair
+
+The imported 1.4.0 generator exposed eight mostly dead or overlapping controls, admitted declared degenerates that its own validator rejected, omitted `RULE_HASH`, rejected canonical examples, and had no executable rival/witness contract. The repair keeps the selected Racket rule unchanged and rebuilds the input sampler around three exact observable controls: grid height, grid width, and template size.
+
+The canonical pairs are also consistent with a plausible shortcut: rotate five-cell templates by 180 degrees, otherwise reflect left-to-right. Canonical five-cell templates are vertically symmetric, so rotation and horizontal reflection agree there. Generated five-cell templates are required to be vertically asymmetric, and every consecutive five-pair schedule window contains at least two such witnesses; therefore every permitted single-query rotation leaves a witness in the demonstrations.
+
